{{Quote|That's just Teedo&mdash;he wants you for parts. He's no respect for anyone.|Rey after rescuing BB-8 from Teedo|<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>}}
'''Teedos''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Reptile|reptilian]] [[species]] native to the [[planet]] [[Jakku]], in the [[Western Reaches]]. They were diminutive in height and had [[Color|gray-green]] skin, most of which was covered in wrappings to protect them from the intense heat of their homeworld.

Teedos made no distinction between individuals, and so each member of the species was simply named Teedo. The species experienced an unknown form of telepathic connection between individuals, and Teedo were known to recall events that happened to other Teedo. They spoke a language called [[Teedospeak]]. They worshiped a [[Deity|goddess]] named [[R'iia]], and believed the violent storms on Jakku were her breath, or ''[[X'us'R'iia]]''.

==Biology and appearance==
Teedo were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Reptile|reptilian]] [[species]] that had scaly [[Color|gray-green]] skin.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> They averaged 28 [[kilogram]]s in weight<ref name="TFA head to head" /> and 1.24 [[meter]]s in height.<ref name="Teedo" /> Although much of their bodies was covered in wrappings and a mask, they had an exposed cranial dome and hands and feet with three digits.<ref name="Visual">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> They made their homes in [[desert]]s or wastelands<ref name="VE" /> and due to the limited [[water]] of their [[homeworld]], [[Jakku]], they had a system of filters and tubes which reclaimed most of their bodies' water for recycling.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

It appeared that they experienced an unknown form of telepathic communication between individuals, and Teedo could know things that were experienced by other Teedo.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

==History==
The origin of Teedos was unknown. Some [[scholar]]s believed that the species evolved on Jakku, while others argued they migrated from another [[star system]].<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

==Society and culture==
Fiercely territorial, Teedos lived as [[scavenger]]s,<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> and they prowled the wastes of Jakku.<ref name="Teedo" /> They were secretive and suspicious of outsiders, often fighting with other scavengers over machinery that could be salvaged for sale. As scavengers, they were capable mechanics and tinkerers, and were gifted in finding useful things in their homeworld. They were treated with respectful caution by the residents of Jakku, due to their unpredictable nature.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

[[File:Teedo_Luggabeast.png|thumb|left|300px|Teedos often rode luggabeasts.]]
In order to protect themselves against Jakku's heat, Teedos wore protective wrappings that covered much of their bodies. They made no distinction between individuals, and none had names, with each being known simply as Teedo. They often rode [[luggabeast]]s, beasts of burden that were [[Cybernetics|cybernetically]] enhanced for greater endurance. Teedos carried [[ionization spear]]s which could [[stun]] or [[Death|kill]].<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" /> They lived in trapdoor tunnel systems.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

Their [[language]] was [[Teedospeak]], and they worshiped a [[Deity|goddess]] named [[R'iia]], believing the violent storms on Jakku were her breath, or ''[[X'us'R'iia]]''.<ref name="BeforetheAwakening">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref> The Teedos had a relationship with the [[Sitter]], whom they brought food and water to. A teedo would always chase away the crowds that gathered around the sitter if they annoyed him.<ref name="Survival">''[[Rey's Survival Guide]]''</ref>

==Teedo in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Give me that&hellip;I did just save your life.|Rey reclaims her bag from Teedo|<ref name="Run Rey Run">{{FOD|Run Rey Run}}</ref>}}
Shortly before the [[Battle of Jakku]], former [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebellion]] member [[Brentin Lore Wexley]] and former [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]] asked some Teedos if they knew anything regarding the mysterious head of the [[Shadow Council]], [[Gallius Rax]], who they were attempting to locate. They knew nothing of use.<ref name="Empire's End" />

In the [[New Republic]] [[New Republic Era|era]], a [[Teedo (Niima Outpost)|Teedo]] operated near a [[Starship Graveyard]], there in the wake of the battle of Jakku. In [[34 ABY]], he had captured the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]], but it was rescued by fellow scavenger [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]]. The next morning, Teedo and two other bandits attempted to steal BB-8 from Rey as they left her [[Hellhound Two|home]] for [[Niima Outpost]]. Rey was able to escape Teedo by forcing him to follow her into a crashed [[Star Destroyer]], where his [[speeder bike]] was eaten by a [[nightwatcher worm]].<ref name="BB-8 Bandits">{{FOD|BB-8 Bandits}}</ref> He wore a mask, and like many Teedo, he rode a luggabeast.<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
Teedos were created with the Niima Outpost Teedo for the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']].<ref name="TFA" /> They first were shown and named by ''Entertainment Weekly'' in an exclusive digital trading card. For ''The Force Awakens'', Teedo was portrayed by [[Kiran Shah]] in a suit, and voiced by [[David Acord]].<ref name="Name Confirmations">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/article/2015/08/12/star-wars-force-awakens-character-names/2|text=''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'': J.J. Abrams explains what's in a name|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2015-08-12|archivedate=20191122201959}}</ref>

